# Website design system

Before writing or changing any website UI, read [`DESIGN-Guide.md`](DESIGN-Guide.md) and follow it. That file is the source of truth for tokens, type, radius, components, and do/don'ts. Do not invent a parallel palette, type scale, or component language.

## Surface and color

- Default page surface is canvas white (`#ffffff`). Dark product bands are deep green (`#003c33`) or navy (`#071829`), full-width — not mid-tone page backgrounds.
- Primary CTA is near-black (`#17171c`) on light, white on dark. Coral (`#ff7759`) is editorial taxonomy only, never the main CTA or a broad fill.
- Action blue (`#1863dc`) is for links and editorial emphasis, not decorative surfaces.
- Keep UI shells flat. No card drop shadows. Gradients are media-led only (hero imagery, product films), never generic section fills.

## Type

- Display: CohereText (fallback Space Grotesk / Inter). Body/UI: Unica77 (fallback Inter). Labels: CohereMono.
- One oversized headline per page, then 16–24px UI copy. Weight 400 almost everywhere; size and contrast do hierarchy, not bold.
- Display tracking is tight and negative. Do not collapse display/body into one generic sans.

## Shape and layout

- Primary buttons: pill (`32px`), 14px/500, padding `12px 24px`.
- Major media cards: `22px` radius. Product/blog cards: `8px`. Do not use <8px on major media.
- Whitespace is a trust signal. Prefer unframed rows, hairline rules (`#d9d9dd`), and open space over wrapping every block in a card.
- Nav: logo left, menu center, CTA right.

## Components to reuse, not reinvent

Match names in `DESIGN-Guide.md`: `button-primary`, `button-secondary` (underlined text, no fill), `hero-photo-card`, `agent-console-card`, `trust-logo-strip`, `dark-feature-band`, `product-card`, `capability-card`.

```tsx
// BAD — generic SaaS chrome
<button className="rounded-md bg-blue-600 shadow-lg">Get started</button>

// GOOD — primary pill on white canvas
<button className="rounded-[32px] bg-[#17171c] px-6 py-3 text-[14px] font-medium text-white">
  Request a demo
</button>
```
